error[ffi_not_constant]: `fixedbugs-2101-statement.h` has `ST_SIDE`, but not as a constant — clang cannot read its value while compiling
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2101-a-statement-expression-computed-when-read-is-told-not-constant.hero:21:5
     |
  21 |     constant ST_SIDE: i32  #~ ffi_not_constant
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: a `constant` names one value forever (§4.4), and clang reads `ST_SIDE` as something computed each time it is read, an object, a call or a statement expression it does not fold, so nothing holds two reads of it to one answer: the mutable global §4.2 forbids. A value computed in C is reached through a function of the program's own that returns it, written in a header beside this file and bound by `extern` naming that header like any function: `static inline <its C type> hero_ST_SIDE(void) { return ST_SIDE; }`

